body:
Before the switch, I made a checklist and clicked through both tables with the same data. Gaps found in table-v3:

1. column reordering by drag is missing;
2. the saved column widths use another storage key, so users lose their widths once;
3. the status badge colors differ from the dark theme palette;
4. the print view of the table is empty, as the virtual window renders only 30 rows;
5. the right-click copy of a cell is gone;
6. the CSV export button is not wired to the new filter state.

Points 2 and 3 are quick. For the width key, I added a one-time migration from the old key. The badge colors now come from the theme tokens, and I checked them on the dark theme.

Point 4 needs a decision. Printing 20k rows is not sensible anyway, so the print view will print the current filtered result up to 1000 rows and show a note if there are more. I will ask Jonas whether dispatchers print at all.

Point 6 is the one with risk. The export reads the table's filter state, which in the new version lives in the URL, so I connected the button to the parsed query. The export itself is unchanged and still builds the file in memory, so large selections remain slow.

Drag reorder and copy come next, in this order.
